pysisyphus 1.0.0: 0005-irc-external-stop-rule

What: IRC accepts stop_func: called after every step; when it returns a true value the direction ends as converged. The runs pass the project stopping rule (|ΔE| < 0.05 kJ/mol per step for 20 steps after the last bond event, pipeline/steps.irc_stop_index) and switch pysisyphus's own stops off (rms_grad_thresh=1e-12, energy_thresh=−1).
Test: SN2 validation path: both sides ended by this rule, ends −0.005 and +0.322 kJ/mol from the optimized minima (true_irc2/final_final_gs_s005.md); patched package = run code on a model potential (stand-in rule).

